00:01:04.010 --> 00:01:05.218
- Well don’t believe me?

00:01:05.220 --> 00:01:06.510
Check this out.

00:01:06.511 --> 00:01:07.886
- Hi, my name’s Dr. Julie Foster,

00:01:07.888 --> 00:01:09.223
and I am a chiropractor.

00:01:12.018 --> 00:01:14.060
So text neck is really a syndrome,

00:01:14.061 --> 00:01:16.061
which just means that
it’s a group of symptoms

00:01:16.063 --> 00:01:17.980
that we’ve developed specifically

00:01:17.981 --> 00:01:20.733
from the way that we
hold our media devices.

00:01:20.735 --> 00:01:22.360
Our cell phones, specifically.

00:01:22.361 --> 00:01:25.030
Well the symptoms can vary
from person to person,

00:01:25.031 --> 00:01:27.240
but it’s really common to find patients

00:01:27.241 --> 00:01:29.408
who complain of neck pain, for sure,

00:01:29.410 --> 00:01:33.036
shoulder pain, headaches, tension,

00:01:33.038 --> 00:01:34.663
and definitely difficulty
in the way that they’re

00:01:34.665 --> 00:01:36.583
able to turn their heads.

00:01:36.585 --> 00:01:38.793
When you keep leaning your head forward

00:01:38.795 --> 00:01:40.711
we pull it out of that natural position.

00:01:40.713 --> 00:01:42.130
Normally everybody’s head
weighs, I don’t know,

00:01:42.131 --> 00:01:44.381
10 or 12 pounds depending
on how smart you are,

00:01:44.383 --> 00:01:47.093
but the further you go away from your body

00:01:47.095 --> 00:01:50.596
the more force that your
head applies to your neck.

00:01:50.598 --> 00:01:52.890
So as I pitch more and more forward

00:01:52.891 --> 00:01:55.226
my head becomes, literally, heavier.

00:01:55.228 --> 00:01:58.938
Up to weights like two and
three, maybe six, times

00:01:58.940 --> 00:02:01.023
its normal weight, so this
is really significant strain

00:02:01.025 --> 00:02:02.401
over long periods of time.

00:02:06.321 --> 00:02:07.155
