in the Bahamas or something.

00:10:17.020 --> 00:10:18.855
I mean, there are a
million things we would do.

00:10:18.856 --> 00:10:20.731
- I feel like I’d stick
around for a while.

00:10:20.733 --> 00:10:22.108
- Oh, totally, totally.

00:10:22.110 --> 00:10:22.900
- Learn every instrument.

00:10:22.901 --> 00:10:24.151
- Of course, you’d be an expert!

00:10:24.153 --> 00:10:25.695
I’d wanna be an astronaut, I’d wanna be

00:10:25.696 --> 00:10:27.363
a professional surfer.
- So let’s talk about

00:10:27.365 --> 00:10:28.865
the Transhumanist party.

00:10:28.866 --> 00:10:32.160
- We’re a small political
party founded about a year ago.

00:10:32.161 --> 00:10:35.036
Broadly the community is interested in

00:10:35.038 --> 00:10:37.790
using politics as a means to further

00:10:37.791 --> 00:10:39.291
the Transhumanist agenda.

00:10:39.293 --> 00:10:41.710
Which is just to say, let’s
promote science and technology

00:10:41.711 --> 00:10:44.838
more instead of, for example,
spending trillions of dollars

00:10:44.840 --> 00:10:47.591
on far-off wars; why not
have the American government

00:10:47.593 --> 00:10:50.093
spend all that money on a war on cancer?

00:10:50.095 --> 00:10:52.053
I mean, this is really what
my presidential campaign is

00:10:52.055 --> 00:10:54.681
about is just trying to
make waves, trying to enter

00:10:54.683 --> 00:10:56.850
the national conversation and say,

00:10:56.851 --> 00:10:58.936
“Hey, don’t you think we can do better?

00:10:58.938 --> 00:11:00.563
“Don’t you think we can spend money

00:11:00.565 --> 00:11:02.606
on our health, on our longevity?”

00:11:02.608 --> 00:11:05.485
Slowly we can overcome
any kind of disaster,

00:11:05.486 --> 00:11:08.070
any kind of problem that
we have as a species,

00:11:08.071 --> 00:11:10.656
by putting in these bionics, or robotics,

00:11:10.658 --> 00:11:13.408
or 3D printed organs that will help us

00:11:13.410 --> 00:11:15.828
become a much stronger species.

00:11:15.830 --> 00:11:17.246
This is really important, for example,

00:11:17.248 --> 00:11:19.998
imagine if the dinosaurs
had the bionic lung?

00:11:20.000 --> 00:11:21.166
They might have survived.

00:11:21.168 --> 00:11:23.418
- That would have been bad for us, though.

00:11:23.420 --> 00:11:24.461
- Yes, very bad for us.

00:11:24.463 --> 00:11:26.338
